/-!
# Weakly associated primes and restriction of scalars

All rings are commutative with unit and `Spec(R)` denotes the set of prime ideals of a
ring `R`. For a ring `R`, an `R`-module `M` and `m ∈ M`, the annihilator of `m` is the
ideal `Ann_R(m) = {f ∈ R | f • m = 0}`, and a prime `p ⊆ R` is *weakly associated* to `M`
if there exists `m ∈ M` such that `p` is minimal among the prime ideals containing
`Ann_R(m)` (Stacks tag 0547). The set of these primes is `WeakAss_R(M) ⊆ Spec(R)`, here
`weaklyAssociatedPrimes R M`, and `Ann_R(m)` is the annihilator `(R ∙ m).annihilator` of
the cyclic submodule generated by `m`.

A ring map `φ : R → S` induces `Spec(φ) : Spec(S) → Spec(R)` sending a prime `q ⊆ S` to
its contraction `φ⁻¹(q) = Ideal.comap φ q`, so that `Spec(φ)(T) = Ideal.comap φ '' T` for
`T ⊆ Spec(S)`. It also makes an `S`-module `M` into an `R`-module by restriction of
scalars, `r • m = φ r • m`, which is `Module.compHom M φ`.

Stacks tag 05C6 (Lemma 10.66.11): for a ring map `φ : R → S` and an `S`-module `M`
regarded as an `R`-module along `φ`, one has
`Spec(φ)(WeakAss_S(M)) ⊇ WeakAss_R(M)`, i.e. every `p ∈ WeakAss_R(M)` is of the form
`φ⁻¹(q)` for some `q ∈ WeakAss_S(M)`. The proof rests on the identity
`Ann_R(m) = φ⁻¹(Ann_S(m))`, after which a minimal prime over `Ann_S(m)` contracting to `p`
is supplied by `Ideal.exists_minimalPrimes_comap_eq`.

The reverse inclusion does not hold in general (Stacks tag 05C5, Remark 10.66.10), so this
is genuinely a one-sided containment.
-/

@[expose] public section

open scoped Pointwise

/-- Stacks tag 05C6 (Lemma 10.66.11): for a ring map `φ : R → S` and an `S`-module `M`
regarded as an `R`-module by restriction of scalars along `φ`, every prime of `R` weakly
associated to `M` is the contraction along `φ` of a prime of `S` weakly associated
to `M`. -/
@[stacks 05C6, ega "IV 3.1.10.1" "Lifting inclusion"]
theorem weakAss_subset_image_comap
    {R S : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S] (φ : R →+* S)
    {M : Type*} [AddCommGroup M] [Module S M] :
    letI : Module R M := Module.compHom M φ
    weaklyAssociatedPrimes R M ⊆ (Ideal.comap φ) '' (weaklyAssociatedPrimes S M) := by
  let : Module R M := Module.compHom M φ
  intro p hp
  -- `hp : IsWeaklyAssociatedPrime R M p`, i.e. there is `m` with
  -- `p ∈ (R ∙ m).annihilator.minimalPrimes`.
  obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ := hp
  -- The R-annihilator of `m` is the contraction of the S-annihilator.
  have hann : (R ∙ m).annihilator = ((S ∙ m).annihilator).comap φ := by
    ext r
    rw [Ideal.mem_comap, Submodule.mem_annihilator_span_singleton,
        Submodule.mem_annihilator_span_singleton]
    change r • m = 0 ↔ φ r • m = 0
    rfl
  rw [hann] at hm
  -- Find a minimal prime of the S-annihilator contracting to `p`.
  obtain ⟨q, hq, hqp⟩ := Ideal.exists_minimalPrimes_comap_eq φ p hm
  exact ⟨q, ⟨m, hq⟩, hqp⟩
